Things to Fix:
  ☐ Add behaviour settings per channel
  ☐ Force branching before response
  ☐ Read category descriptions from DESCRIPTION.md, not index.md (skills.rs
    load_category_description). DESCRIPTION.md is the ecosystem convention —
    the OpenClaw migration path we claim compat with writes it, and portable
    skill trees ship it. Accept both, prefer DESCRIPTION.md. Categories from
    an imported tree currently load with empty descriptions.
  ☐ Skill index renders one skill as 5 indented XML lines (<skill><name>
    <description>). On a 121-skill catalog that is 22.6k chars to carry 9.7k of
    names and descriptions — 57% markup, 107 chars overhead per skill, and 54%
    of the whole system prompt. Flatten the leaf to `- name: description`
    under the existing category grouping: 9.8k saved, no information lost.
  ☐ HUMAN.md renders into the org context uncapped — a 9k profile is 9k of
    prompt on every turn. Budget it with an inline utilization header
    (valid there: store = render for authored docs), and cap the other
    unbounded sections (skill index, projects, channels) as plain limits.
    View blocks (memory render, working memory, participants) report scope
    + shown-of-total counts instead of fill — a view always fills its
    budget by selection, so a percentage is meaningless there.
  ☐ Skill loader only descends one category level. Skills at
    {category}/{subcategory}/{name} (e.g. mlops/inference/llama-cpp) are
    silently dropped — a 126-skill tree renders 120. Recurse and render the
    subcategory as its own grouping, or flatten to "category/subcategory".
  ☐ DESCRIPTION_BUDGET (80) truncates the bundled wiki-writing description at
    183 chars, cutting its routing signal mid-word. Either raise the budget or
    fix the bundled skill — but the budget is unenforced on load, so imported
    trees hit this too (~26% of a 126-skill tree).

